d8f43af6bca68d54cedbfb6a360dad4bf2d6b12da508cfee75cd0f","solve/challenge.json":"93882929a198ceaade16f9c1b1811106dca5c7151d85fc8f526a9d913f8feafb","solve/solution.py":"e790744e59d8f43af6bca68d54cedbfb6a360dad4bf2d6b12da508cfee75cd0f","solve/source/generator.py":"66a3c56f61986c75dc40053dce167a0b6f0c513892a78de98ba521379d7809ac","solve/summary.json":"c5ebe2c4c9bdfa77a1af837a7f705557cffa8d908705e7dd6bd4134dbcacf2de"},"feedback_items":[{"id":"F1","text":"Highest priority — add declared-parameter lesson identifiability to `lesson-census`\n\n**Symptom.** Existing rule labels can all be correct while a hidden parameter is absent from every demonstration and changes only the query. Per-grid correctness and marginal witness frequency do not catch that training defect.\n\n**Concrete example.** The task-local `projection_span` prototype must reject an episode where span 1 and span 2 agree on all three demos but disagree on the held-out query. See `checks/parametric/projection-span-evidence.json` and `repo/generators/b19deac47327/workspace/parametric/prototype.py`.\n\n**Suggested change.** Let generators declare a small parameter/rival matrix whose alternatives are executable Racket programs or callable rule IDs. In `arcpuzzles lesson-census`, compare per-pair output hashes and report/block `all demos equal + query differs`, including the exact episode, query holdout, source hashes, and equivalence-class opt-out. This is the shared-tool change most likely to improve Qwen3.5-9B data value."},{"id":"F2","text":"Automatically enumerate a declared lesson period in the standard strict after battery\n\n**Symptom.** The duties’ ordinary after command produced 11/12 green on the final source because the semantic gate required period enumeration, even though the generator declares `LESSON_SCHEDULE_PERIOD = 4`. The successful rerun needed extra flags not present in the standard command.\n\n**Concrete example.** Compare `checks/after/` with `checks/after-enumerated/`; the generator hash is identical (`66a3c56f…`).\n\n**Suggested change.** When strict after/audit mode sees a small positive `LESSON_SCHEDULE_PERIOD`, automatically enumerate it at a pinned seed, or emit a ready-to-run exact command and classify the first result as incomplete rather than a semantic source failure. Preserve an explicit opt-out for large or stochastic schedules."},{"id":"F3","text":"Make audit task-test portability failures first-class and separate from semantic findings\n\n**Symptom.** The `6b5d8752c5c4` audit preset exposed a focused test that resolves canonical data through a fixed `__file__.parents[...]` depth. It fails in the portable runtime before testing generator semantics, while the same audit also lacks a semantic contract.\n\n**Concrete example.** `checks/audit/6b5d8752c5c4/audit-check.log` reports the missing portable canonical path and the separate semantic-contract failure.\n\n**Suggested change.** Give audit summaries distinct fields for `portable_test_preflight`, `task_test_result`, and `semantic_contract_result`, and offer a linter autofix hint using `reviewer_support.find_root`, `canonical_path`, and `canonical_pairs`. That prevents a path-layout bug from being conflated with an adversarial semantic result."}],"packet_id":"ee835cf31b5faa0498e135f699e5f09949b0bd6bf3b943d18a7a0a0152610e41","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"61a5d69dd325c6d0580ea40a31baac0a5e463b53b6bd382f6f9190a145dc9d7e","instance_hash":"8152e93c03b460aa8d00b9fcc0ff83d66b2fe616c5a0fdf850a912055195ff91","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"solve_kind":"blind_before_repair","source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished","task_id":"1bc816e1eb99"},"reviewer_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve/a